00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.090
So shadowing is a language learning
technique that I believe was developed by

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.805
professor Argüelles,  alexander Argüelles,
and you can Google for him, shadowing

00:00:32.805 --> 00:00:34.725
Alexander Argüelles or Argüelles.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:38.775
And you'll find a number of videos
that he's put out on the subject.

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:45.675
The gist of it is that as a means of
improving your pronunciation and preparing

00:00:45.675 --> 00:00:52.995
for output you can, while listening to
something, you can try to speak along like

00:00:53.025 --> 00:00:55.295
imitate what you hear, copy what you hear.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:59.760
Even if you drop the odd word or
the odd syllable, and this is a

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.940
practice in, I guess, focusing
in on what you're listening to

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.440
imitating their pronunciation.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.750
And I have tried it in the past and
I found that it was not something

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.490
that I was able to continue with.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:13.710
I just wasn't motivated to do it.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.080
I preferred, you know, the more relaxed
approach of either, you know, at, at an

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.770
early stage, in my learning, listening
to repetitive material, like the mini

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.350
stories or as I progressed to things of
more interest to me, I would focus in

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.350
on the content, what I was listening to.

00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:36.690
And I wasn't really that keen on
sort of almost interrupting the

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:42.270
flow of listening to whatever I was
listening to by trying to, uh, say,

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.889
you know, to imitate what I heard.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:49.309
However, uh, I'm willing to
try anything, uh, if it's

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.580
effective for language learning.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:53.154
And I thought that, you know, A.

00:01:53.205 --> 00:01:56.774
I thought I will do a video on
shadowing and then I said to myself,

00:01:56.774 --> 00:01:59.384
well, you were kind of negative on
